p.src:
For the antisymmetric tensor, an infinitesimal transformation acts on either index: $\delta\Psi^{ij}
=
i\epsilon
\left(
T^i{}_k\Psi^{kj}
+
T^j{}_k\Psi^{ik}
\right).$ In the matrix picture, the first term moves vertically and the second moves horizontally. The constituent labels used to build the tensor are only a mnemonic; Eq. [eq:l10-two-index-action] is the exact group-theoretic statement.

