p.src:
Below the unification threshold the symmetry is broken, the light spectrum does not fill complete degenerate $SU(5)$ multiplets, and the three beta-function coefficients differ. Consequently the couplings run at different rates. At the high scale one asks whether they reach a common value: $\alpha_1(M_{\mathrm{GUT}})
\stackrel{?}{=}
\alpha_2(M_{\mathrm{GUT}})
\stackrel{?}{=}
\alpha_3(M_{\mathrm{GUT}}).$

